{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Y47SZqENvXVggVYTXDAwo","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nWhen a worker's branch is pushed but opening the pull request fails, the PR should be retried, and later re-opened, from the recorded close-out without running the agent again. The work touches the worker loop and close-out, the job record, retry classification, the built-in worker prompt template and the proposal. engineer is the only triage role in this repository, so it plans the steps.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: plan the change to the job record (pushed head, test result, PR body), the retryable cause, CreatePR retry with backoff, the agent-free re-open path, dry-run behaviour, GitHub-fake tests and the proposal update.\n- worker engineer: Go change in internal/worker (and related effects and github fake code), plus tests and docs.\n\n## Open issues\n- The issue also asks the worker prompt to handle a branch that already holds the finished work. The worker may edit the built-in template at internal/roles/workers/engineer/prompt.txt. The deployed copy at .ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt is a protected path, so agents may not change it. A maintainer has to sync that copy by hand.\n- The change adds fields to the stored job record, and no architect role exists to review that. The engineer plan should cover compatibility with job records that already exist.\n- The retry classification depends on the shared transient-error handling from the related push-retry issue. The engineer should check whether that has landed or must be built here.\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\n# Loop poll intervals. Unset loops keep their defaults (scanners 4h, triage\n# 15m, workers 5m, reviewers 5m, prwatch 5m); 1m is the minimum. Hand-offs\n# no longer wait for a poll: a close-out wakes the next loop, a freed slot\n# wakes loops with waiting work, and approvals and unblocks are watched every\n# minute (#394, #406). The merger is controller code with no agent or job\n# slot, so it polls every minute to merge green PRs sooner.\nintervals: { merger: 1m }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make lint test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\ninternal:\nagent\nagentjob\nbotcheck\nbudget\ncli\ncloseout\ncommitter\nconfig\nconfigcmd\nconfigsrc\ncontroller\ncostblock\ncosts\ndigest\ndocscheck\neffects\nexecutor\ngithub\ngitref\ngitx\nimagescan\ninitcmd\nintake\njanitor\njobexe