{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MP8TtbckoUL8yLbPWrtaM","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\npackage worker\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/closeout\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/committer\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tmaxQuoteRunes     = 4000\n\tsummaryWithheld   = \"Summary withheld by the secret scan.\"\n\tsummaryNone       = \"The agent wrote no summary.\"\n\ttestsRanOutOfTime = \"ran out of time\"\n)\n\n// Title is the PR title: the first line of the code commit message.\nfunc Title(typ, issueTitle string, issue int, jobID string) (string, error) {\n\tmsg, err := committer.CodeMessage(typ, issueTitle, issue, \"\", jobID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tfirst, _, _ := strings.Cut(msg, \"\\n\")\n\treturn first, nil\n}\n\n// QuoteSummary renders agent text for a PR body: closing references\n// neutralised (including the HTML-entity and backslash forms of \"#\"), ard\n// markers and @-mentions defused, cut to 4,000 runes and quoted. The text must\n// already be redacted.\nfunc QuoteSummary(s string) string {\n\ts = strings.TrimSpace(strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"\\r\", \"\"))\n\tif s == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"> \" + summaryNone\n\t}\n\ts = closeout.Sanitize(committer.NeutraliseRefs(s))\n\tif r := []rune(s); len(r) > maxQuoteRunes {\n\t\ts = strings.TrimRight(string(r[:maxQuoteRunes]), \"\\n\") + \"\\n… (truncated; full text in the committed file)\"\n\t}\n\tlines := strings.Split(s, \"\\n\")\n\tfor i, l := range lines {\n\t\tlines[i] = strings.TrimRight(\"> \"+l, \" \")\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n// BodyInfo is what the PR body is made of.\ntype BodyInfo struct {\n\tRepo    github.Repo\n\tIssue   int\n\tRole    string\n\tBranch  string\n\tJobID   string\n\tSummary string // redacted agent text; \"\" when withheld or absent\n\t// Withheld says the secret scan held the summary back.\n\tWithheld bool\n\tResult   closeout.WorkerResult\n}\n\n// Body renders the PR body. The only closing reference in it is ard's own\n// \"Closes #<issue>\", written here and never passed through NeutraliseRefs.\nfunc Body(b BodyInfo) string {\n\tvar w strings.Builder\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"Closes #%d\\n\\n\", b.Issue)\n\tplan := fmt.Sprintf(\"https://github.com/%s/%s/blob/main/.ard/%d/plan.md\", b.Repo.Owner, b.Repo.Name, b.Issue)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"Opened by ard from issue #%d. The summary below was written by an agent and is untrusted; the [plan](%s) came from triage.\\n\\n\", b.Issue, plan)\n\tif b.Withheld {\n\t\tw.WriteString(\"> \" + summaryWithheld + \"\\n\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tw.WriteString(QuoteSummary(b.Summary) + \"\\n\")\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"\\n**Tests:** %s\\n\", testsText(b.Result))\n\tif b.Result.Large != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"\\n**%s**\\n\", b.Result.Large)\n\t}\n\tif len(b.Result.Fetched) > 0 {\n\t\tw.WriteString(\"\\n**Fetched inputs:**\\n\\n\")\n\t\tfor _, f := range b.Result.Fetched {\n\t\t\tby := \"`\" + f.VerifiedBy + \"`\"\n\t\t\tif f.VerifiedBy == \"none\" {\n\t\t\t\tby = \"none (unverified)\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"- `%s` → `%s` · sha256 `%s` · verified by %s\\n\", f.URL, f.Path, f.SHA256, by)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tbase := fmt.Sprintf(\"https://github.com/%s/%s\", b.Repo.Owner, b.Repo.Name)\n\trole := fmt.Sprintf(\".ard/%d/worker-%s.md\", b.Issue, b.Role)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(&w, \"\\n**Files:** [%s](%s/blob/%s/%s) · [logs](%s/tree/%s/.ard/%d/logs) · job `%s`\\n\",\n\t\trole, base, b.Branch, role, base, b.Branch, b.Issue, b.JobID)\n\treturn w.String()\n}\n\nfunc testsText(r closeout.WorkerResult) string {\n\tfixes := \"\"\n\tswitch r.Fixes {\n\tcase 0:\n\tcase 1:\n\t\tfixes = \" after 1 fix attempt\"\n\tdefault:\n\t\tfixes = fmt.Sprintf(\" after %d fix attempts\", r.Fixes)\n\t}\n\tswitch r.Tests {\n\tcase closeout.TestsPassed:\n\t\treturn \"passed\" + fixes\n\tcase closeout.TestsFailed:\n\t\ts := \"failed\" + fixes\n\t\tif r.TestNote != \"\" {\n\t\t\ts += \" (\" + r.TestNote + \")\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn s\n\t}\n\treturn \"not configured\"\n}\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds a transient error class to gitx, a separate bounded backoff retry in the committer's main, code and init lanes that checks whether the push already landed, and a new retryable close-out cause. Size M to L, risk medium because the shared retry loop and the close-out mapping change.\n\n## Open issues\n- No existing close-out cause fits, so the plan adds a new one, `push_transient`. A maintainer may prefer another name.\n- The protected-branch rejection case from the comment is left out of this change. Its retry count and needs-human wording are a policy decision, so it should be a separate issue.\n- A job that is already a retry gets no further automatic retry. The plan flags that such a job must still not end as executor-failed. The worker should check this against the close-out plan logic.\n- The lane holds its semaphore during backoff, which can delay other commits on the same branch for up to about a minute.\n0a355a9 ard(triage:engineer): #357 Adds a transient error class to gitx, a separate bounded backoff retry… [skip ci]\n090940a ard(triage:lead): #357 The committer should retry transient push failures, such as server erro… [skip ci]\n71de398 feat: Reviewer selection rules (#42) (#209)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59f13bd1-4af6-4d3c-a6ca-3a44112790d5","uuid":"898e6324-b95e-4561-8d3a-cc05ef35e44c","timestamp":"2026-11-25T16:52:02.138Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\npackage worker\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/closeout\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/committer\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tmaxQuoteRunes     = 4000\n\tsummaryWithheld   = \"Summary withheld by the secret scan.\"\n\tsummaryNone  