{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S24zmqqwJdNZV24M5S91XZ","type":"tool_result","content":"// failedPlan is the plan for a job that did not produce a usable result.\nfunc failedPlan(j Job, reason string, logWithheld bool) Plan {\n\tn := j.target()\n\tp := Plan{Outcome: OutcomeFailed, Reason: reason, LogWithheld: logWithheld,\n\t\tTerminal: []Label{{n, labels.ExecutorFailed}},\n\t\tRemove:   []Label{{n, labels.Running(labels.Stage(j.Stage), j.Role)}}}\n\tif logWithheld {\n\t\tp.Terminal = append(p.Terminal, Label{n, labels.NeedsHuman})\n\t}\n\treturn p\n}\n\n// stalePRPlan is the plan for a review whose PR is gone (merged, closed, or its\n// branch deleted). It keeps the review so it is still posted best-effort, but\n// commits nothing and sets no label but removing :running.\nfunc stalePRPlan(p Plan, j Job, why string) Plan {\n\trp := *p.Review\n\trp.PRGone = why\n\treturn Plan{Outcome: OutcomeStale, Status: p.Status, Reason: \"pr gone: \" + why, Summary: p.Summary,\n\t\tReview: &rp, Tail: p.Tail, TailWithheld: p.TailWithheld, KeepUntil: p.KeepUntil,\n\t\tRemove: []Label{{j.target(), labels.Running(labels.Stage(j.Stage), j.Role)}}}\n}\n\n// retryPlan is the plan for a job that failed for a transient cause and hands\n// off to one automatic retry. It removes only :running and leaves the request\n// label alone: a human who removed it to cancel stays cancelled.\nfunc retryPlan(j Job, reason string) Plan {\n\tn := j.target()\n\tst := labels.Stage(j.Stage)\n\treturn Plan{Outcome: OutcomeRetry, Reason: reason,\n\t\tRemove: []Label{{n, labels.Running(st, j.Role)}}}\n}\n\n// limitedPlan is the plan for a job that stopped at a usage limit. It has\n// retryPlan's labels: it removes only :running, leaves the request label alone\n// and adds no terminal label. What differs is the state change (FailLimited)\n// and that it does not touch the automatic retry.\nfunc limitedPlan(j Job, reason string) Plan {\n\tp := retryPlan(j, reason)\n\tp.Outcome = OutcomeLimited\n\treturn p\n}\n\n// needsHumanPlan is the plan for a job held back by the secret scan.\nfunc needsHumanPlan(j Job, status, reason string) Plan {\n\tn := j.target()\n\treturn Plan{Outcome: OutcomeNeedsHuman, Status: status, Reason: reason, LogWithheld: false,\n\t\tTerminal: []Label{{n, labels.NeedsHuman}},\n\t\tRemove:   []Label{{n, labels.Running(labels.Stage(j.Stage), j.Role)}}}\n}\n\nfunc (j Job) validate() error {\n\tswitch j.Stage {\n\tcase StageTriage, StageWorker, StageReview:\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"closeout job %s: stage %q is not triage, worker or review\", j.ID, j.Stage)\n\t}\n\tif j.ID == \"\" || j.Role == \"\" || j.Issue == 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"closeout job %q: id, role and issue are required\", j.ID)\n\t}\n\tif j.Cause.Kind != \"\" {\n\t\t// A job that ended for a known cause commits only its log: it needs\n\t\t// neither a base commit nor a branch (an empty branch puts the log on\n\t\t// main under .ard/<issue#>/logs/).\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tif j.ExitCode == 0 && j.BaseSHA == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"closeout job %s: BaseSHA is required to find the changed files\", j.ID)\n\t}\n\tif j.Stage == StageReview && j.PR == 0 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"closeout job %s: a review needs a PR\", j.ID)\n\t}\n\t// A worker that stops before its first push has no branch: its role file\n\t// and log go to main, as triage's do.\n\tif j.Stage == StageReview && j.Branch == \"\" {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"closeout job %s: a review job needs a branch\", j.ID)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\ninternal/reaper/finish.go:73:func NewCause(sj state.Job, kind closeout.CauseKind, detail string, transient bool) closeout.Cause {\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-74-\treturn closeout.Cause{Kind: kind, Detail: detail, Transient: transient, Retry: transient && sj.RetryOf == \"\"}\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-75-}\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-76-\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-77-// CauseOf decides how a job whose process is no longer running ended. The\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-78-// first rule that matches wins:\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-79-//\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-80-//  1. The Reaper recorded a kill reason: that cause (heartbeat_quiet and\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-81-//     deadline are not transient; controller_restart is).\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-82-//  2. The executor timed the job out: deadline.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-83-//  3. A Gone job with an executor End (Kubernetes): evicted and clone_failed\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-84-//     are transient; prep_failed, bad_result and no_result are no_process.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-85-//  4. The process is gone: controller_restart (transient) when the job was\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-86-//     created before processStart, otherwise no_process. The latter covers a\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-87-//     process of this run that vanished, such as a container killed from\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-88-//     outside.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-89-//  5. The agent reported a transient API error: rate_limit.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-90-//  6. Otherwise the zero Cause: a normal close-out from the role file and the\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-91-//     exit code.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-92-//\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-93-// Retry is set for a transient cause when sj is not itself a retry.\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-94-func CauseOf(sj state.Job, st executor.Status, res agent.Result, processStart time.Time) closeout.Cause {\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-95-\tswitch {\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-96-\tcase sj.KillReason != \"\":\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-97-\t\tkind := closeout.CauseKind(sj.KillReason)\ninternal/reaper/finish.go-98-\t\tswitch kind {\n0005_usage.sql\n0006_cost_tables.sql\n0007_budget.sql\n0008_pr_watch.sql\n30:type Job struct {\n31-\tID            string\n32-\tStage, Role   string\n33-\tIssue, PR     int // Issue is 0 only for stage scanner; PR 0 means none\n34-\tStatus        Status\n35-\tAttempt       int\n36-\tHandle        json.RawMessage /